.hero {{ background: linear-gradient(135deg, #10263d 0%, #16466b 58%, #267c83 100%); color: white; padding: 54px 56px 42px; }}
.hero h1 {{ margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 42px; line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.03em; max-width: 980px; }}
.hero p {{ margin: 0; max-width: 960px; color: #dbe9f4; font-size: 18px; }}
.meta {{ margin-top: 22px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }}
.meta span {{ border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.28); color: #eef8ff; border-radius: 999px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 13px; }}
main {{ max-width: 1180px; margin: -24px auto 48px; padding: 0 24px; }}
.card {{ background: white; border: 1px solid #dce5ee; border-radius: 18px; box-shadow: 0 10px 28px rgba(16, 38, 61, .08); padding: 26px; margin-bottom: 24px; }}
.kpi-grid {{ display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 14px; }}
.kpi {{ background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffffff 0%, #f6f9fc 100%); border: 1px solid #dce5ee; border-radius: 16px; padding: 18px; min-height: 138px; }}
.kpi .label {{ color: var(--slate); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; font-weight: 700; }}
.kpi .value {{ font-size: 31px; font-weight: 800; margin: 8px 0 4px; letter-spacing: -0.04em; color: var(--navy); }}
.kpi .sub {{ color: var(--slate); font-size: 13px; }}
h2 {{ margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 25px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }}
h3 {{ margin: 18px 0 8px; font-size: 16px; }}
p {{ margin: 8px 0 14px; }}
.lead {{ font-size: 17px; color: #33485c; }}
.grid-2 {{ display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr .8fr; gap: 20px; align-items: start; }}
.grid-even {{ display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; }}
.chartbox {{ border: 1px solid #dce5ee; border-radius: 16px; overflow: hidden; background: white; }}
svg {{ width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }}
.chart-title {{ font: 700 18px Inter, Arial, sans-serif; fill: var(--navy); }}
.axis {{ font: 12px Inter, Arial, sans-serif; fill: var(--slate); }}
.axis.small {{ font-size: 11px; }}
.label {{ font-weight: 650; }}
.value {{ font: 700 13px Inter, Arial, sans-serif; fill: var(--navy); }}
.annotation {{ font: 700 13px Inter, Arial, sans-serif; fill: var(--navy); }}
.caption {{ font: 12px Inter, Arial, sans-serif; fill: var(--slate); }}
.bar-label {{ font: 700 12px Inter, Arial, sans-serif; }}
table {{ border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 14px; }}
th, td {{ padding: 10px 11px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5edf4; text-align: right; }}
th:first-child, td:first-child {{ text-align: left; }}
th {{ color: var(--slate); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; background: #f7fafc; }}
.callout {{ background: #f7fafc; border-left: 5px solid var(--teal); border-radius: 12px; padding: 15px 17px; color: #33485c; }}
.method {{ background: #fbfcfe; border: 1px dashed #bfcedd; border-radius: 14px; padding: 14px 16px; color: #40566a; font-size: 14px; }}
ul.insights {{ margin: 8px 0 0 20px; padding: 0; }}
ul.insights li {{ margin: 8px 0; }}
.footer {{ color: #607183; font-size: 13px; text-align: center; margin: 30px 0 0; }}
@media (max-width: 920px) {{ .kpi-grid, .grid-2, .grid-even {{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }} .hero {{ padding: 36px 24px; }} .hero h1 {{ font-size: 32px; }} main {{ margin-top: -12px; }} }}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header class="hero">
  <h1>{html.escape(task['brief']['title'])}</h1>
  <p>{html.escape(task['brief']['one_liner'])}</p>
  <div class="meta">
    <span>Dataset rows: {fmt_int(total)}</span>
    <span>EPOCH range: {epoch_min:%Y-%m-%d} to {epoch_max:%Y-%m-%d}</span>
    <span>Orbit regimes classified by MEAN_MOTION thresholds</span>
  </div>
</header>
<main>
  <section class="card" aria-label="Executive KPI Summary">
    <div class="kpi-grid">
      {''.join(f'<div class="kpi"><div class="label">{html.escape(k)}</div><div class="value">{v}</div><div class="sub">{html.escape(s)}</div></div>' for k, v, s in kpis)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="overview">
    <h2>Catalog Overview & Key Figures</h2>
    <p class="lead">The catalog contains <strong>{fmt_int(total)}</strong> active satellites with TLE epochs from <strong>{epoch_min:%Y-%m-%d}</strong> through <strong>{epoch_max:%Y-%m-%d}</strong>. The median satellite in the dataset has <strong>{fmt_num(mm_median, 2)}</strong> revolutions per day, <strong>{fmt_num(median_incl, 1)}°</strong> inclination, and eccentricity of <strong>{ecc_median:.6f}</strong>.</p>
    <div class="grid-even">
      <div class="chartbox">{svg_histogram(inc_bins, title='Inclination Distribution', color=BLUE)}</div>
      <div class="chartbox">{svg_histogram(mm_bins, title='Mean Motion Distribution (rev/day)', color=TEAL)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="orbit-regime">
    <h2>Orbital Regime Classification</h2>
    <p class="method"><strong>Classification rule:</strong> LEO = MEAN_MOTION &gt; 14 rev/day; GEO = 0.95–1.05 rev/day with ECCENTRICITY &lt; 0.1; HEO = ECCENTRICITY ≥ 0.1 or MEAN_MOTION &lt; 0.95; MEO = remaining satellites between GEO and LEO thresholds. These cutoffs use MEAN_MOTION as the primary discriminator, as required.</p>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="chartbox">{svg_stacked_bar(regime_segments, title='Share of Active Satellites by Orbital Regime')}</div>
      <div>{table_html(['Regime', 'Count', 'Share', 'Median mean motion', 'Median inclination'], regime_rows)}</div>
    </div>
    <p class="callout">LEO accounts for <strong>{fmt_pct(leo_share)}</strong> of the active catalog. Starlink alone represents <strong>{fmt_pct(starlink_share)}</strong> of all satellites and is entirely classified as LEO under the threshold rule, materially shaping the LEO share.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="constellation-analysis">
    <h2>Major Constellation & Operator Breakdown</h2>
    <p class="lead">Constellation labels are parsed from <code>OBJECT_NAME</code> prefixes and common navigation-system name patterns. Starlink dominates the active population with <strong>{fmt_int(starlink_count)}</strong> satellites, exceeding the next named systems by an order of magnitude.</p>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="chartbox">{svg_bar_chart(top_const_chart_data, title='Largest Named Constellations / Systems', x_label='Active satellites')}</div>
      <div>{table_html(['Constellation / system', 'Count', 'Catalog share', 'LEO share within group'], top_const_rows)}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout"><strong>Starlink skew:</strong> Starlink contributes {fmt_int(starlink_count)} of {fmt_int(total)} satellites. With Starlink removed, the remaining catalog has a median inclination of <strong>{fmt_num(nonstar_inc_median, 1)}°</strong>, compared with <strong>{fmt_num(star_inc_median, 1)}°</strong> for Starlink satellites.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="launch-trends">
    <h2>Launch Year Trends</h2>
    <p class="lead">Launch year is extracted from the first four characters of <code>OBJECT_ID</code>. The active fleet is heavily weighted toward recent launches: <strong>{fmt_int(post_2020)}</strong> currently active satellites were launched from 2020 onward, versus <strong>{fmt_int(pre_2020)}</strong> launched before 2020.</p>
    <div class="chartbox">{svg_line_chart(points, title='Currently Active Satellites by Launch Year')}</div>
    <div class="grid-2" style="margin-top:20px;">
      <div class="callout">The peak launch-year cohort in the active catalog is <strong>2025</strong> with <strong>{fmt_int(y2025)}</strong> satellites. The partial 2026 cohort contains <strong>{fmt_int(y2026)}</strong> active satellites in the provided catalog.</div>
      <div>{table_html(['Launch year', 'Active satellites', 'Catalog share'], launch_rows)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="orbital-characteristics">
    <h2>Orbital Parameter Deep Dive</h2>
    <div class="grid-even">
      <div>
        <h3>Inclination shells</h3>
        <p>The inclination distribution clusters strongly around Starlink-like mid-inclination shells and near-polar/sun-synchronous orbits. Satellites with inclinations from 80° to 110° total <strong>{fmt_int(polar)}</strong>, while near-equatorial satellites below 10° total <strong>{fmt_int(equatorial)}</strong>.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Eccentricity profile</h3>
        <p>The median eccentricity is <strong>{ecc_median:.6f}</strong>, indicating that most active satellites are in nearly circular orbits. Satellites with eccentricity ≥ 0.01 total <strong>{fmt_int(ecc_high_001)}</strong>; satellites with eccentricity ≥ 0.1 total <strong>{fmt_int(ecc_high_01)}</strong>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-even">
      <div>{table_html(['Metric', 'Value'], [['Mean motion median', f'{fmt_num(mm_median, 2)} rev/day'], ['Inclination median', f'{fmt_num(median_incl, 1)}°'], ['Eccentricity median', f'{ecc_median:.6f}'], ['Polar-band inclinations (80°–110°)', fmt_int(polar)], ['High eccentricity (≥0.1)', fmt_int(ecc_high_01)]])}</div>
      <div>{table_html(['Segment', 'LEO', 'MEO', 'GEO', 'HEO'], [['Starlink', *(fmt_int(v) for v in star_regime.tolist())], ['Non-Starlink', *(fmt_int(v) for v in nonstar_regime.tolist())]])}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="conclusions">
    <h2>Key Takeaways & Outlook</h2>
    <ul class="insights">
      <li><strong>LEO concentration is the defining orbital-regime fact:</strong> {fmt_int(leo_count)} satellites, or {fmt_pct(leo_share)}, classify as LEO using MEAN_MOTION &gt; 14 rev/day.</li>
      <li><strong>A single constellation dominates totals:</strong> Starlink contains {fmt_int(starlink_count)} satellites, equal to {fmt_pct(starlink_share)} of the full active catalog.</li>
      <li><strong>Launch activity is recent-heavy:</strong> {fmt_int(post_2020)} active satellites have OBJECT_ID launch years of 2020 or later, representing {fmt_pct(post_2020_share)} of the catalog.</li>
      <li><strong>Orbital characteristics are skewed by constellation deployment:</strong> the overall median inclination is {fmt_num(median_incl, 1)}°, while the non-Starlink median is {fmt_num(nonstar_inc_median, 1)}°.</li>
      <li><strong>Policy relevance:</strong> the numbers point to a licensing and coordination environment dominated by LEO constellation density, spectrum demand, and debris-risk management for high-volume deployments.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <div class="footer">Generated from /app/benchmark/data.csv only. No fabricated statistics or placeholder values are included.</div>
</main>
</body>
</html>'''
